class.description:
Store sells what a player buys once and keeps: DLC, expansions, a soundtrack, unlocking the full game. List each item by the game's own ID in the [b]Store[/b] tab of Project Settings, with its product on each store: the DLC's app ID on Steam, the product ID in App Store Connect and in the Play Console. An empty product means the item isn't sold on that store.
[codeblock]
if Store.owns("winter_expansion"):
    unlock_winter_islands()

func _on_buy_pressed():
    var result = await Store.purchase("winter_expansion")
    if not result.ok and result.error != "cancelled":
        show_message(result.message)
[/codeblock]
Store sells through Steam where the game was started from Steam, the App Store on Apple platforms and Google Play on Android. Running from the editor without one, it pretends: the items in [code]store/owned_in_editor[/code] (Project Settings) are owned, and purchases succeed, so both sides of the game can be tried.
Items are never used up: there's no buying coins or gems. The content itself ships with the game (or as a [code].pck[/code] loaded with [method ProjectSettings.load_resource_pack]); Store only says whether the player owns it.
